# Configuration holding credentials. Nothing here is copied into an image
# today -- the Dockerfile's COPY instructions come from web/, db/, app/,
# maint/ and mail/, none from the root -- but this is the safety net: the
# day someone writes `COPY . .`, the MySQL password enters a layer and does
# not come back out even by deleting the file afterwards. Config arrives by
# volume or by environment; see docker-compose.example.yml.
